@startuml per-store-idempotency
title US-11: Idempotency by Logical Fact - Store-Specific Mechanisms

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Position\nConsumer" as PosConsumer
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as CorrWorker
participant "Alert\nEvaluator" as Evaluator
participant "API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as PositionDB
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as AlertsDB

PosConsumer -> PositionDB : INSERT position_history\nON CONFLICT (entity_id, observed_at) DO NOTHING

note over PositionDB
  Position logical identity is entity + source event time.
  observed_at is deterministically derived from timestamp_ms.
end note

PosConsumer -> Redis : read stored last_seen_ms
Redis --> PosConsumer : stored timestamp or nil
alt incoming timestamp newer than stored
  PosConsumer -> Redis : write latest live state
else duplicate/stale event
  PosConsumer -> PosConsumer : skip live-state regression/redundant update
end

CorrWorker -> CorrWorker : pair_key = min(a,b):max(a,b)\nepisode_id = pair_key:episode_start_ms
CorrWorker -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT\nON deterministic episode identity

Evaluator -> Evaluator : derive type-specific deterministic alert_id
Evaluator -> API : via Kafka alerts\n(same logical alert may be replayed)
API -> AlertsDB : INSERT alert\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over Evaluator, AlertsDB
  Alert identity is type-specific.
  Pair-based alerts include pair_key.
  Durable DB effect is idempotent;
  Kafka transport remains at-least-once.
end note

@enduml
